{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1114225-silly-thought-but-i-want-to-make-a-mage-that-is-in-a-musical","id":1114225,"title":"Silly Thought But... I want to make a mage that is in a musical","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-10T11:45:43-07:00","id":1114225,"title":"Silly Thought But... I want to make a mage that is in a musical","content":"So like the title says I want my Mage to be in a musical and to have the whole world act in accordance. Like other people can sing, and maybe he should give buffs to things if they do, but you get the whole back up dancer thing going on, and you have the fact that a large portion of the does doesn't seem to notice it going on. <br /> <br /> This is where you come in... I need help figuring out what Arcana I need at what levels to pull this off. I figure I probably need Fate, Mind, and Space (Isolation will either have folks backing off or ignoring me)... probably want forces as well unless... I guess I could use Mind to produce the actual music.<br /> <br /> Help me Mage Forums...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8432-resilientcomma","name":"ResilientComma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T12:51:45-07:00","id":1114246,"title":"","content":"Well for starters you ought to get a Shadow Name relating to music/musicals in some way and your Long-Term Nimbus will take care of a lot of the basic theming. In terms of Arcana, Mind is pretty much mandatory to press people into service as background characters. Ideally at 4 dots so you could use Gain Skill to make your backup dancers/singers actually competent, but assuming basic character creation rules you'll have to stick to 3 dots and hope they took choir in high school so you can use Enhance Skill. Maybe make your Nimubs Tilt +1 Expression so you have something to work with?<br /> <br /> Other than that the only obvious thing is Forces to become a living stage (lights, sounds, pyrotechnics etc.), but any of the Arcana might prove useful. Fate to assure a succesful career, Time to get things set up in a flash, Matter to make props and costumes, Space to project your performance and keep the haters off the stage, Life to become really, really, ridiculously good looking, Prime to build enchanted instruments, Spirit to nurture a brood of spirits of performance/ecstacy/music, Death if you want use ghosts and shadow for darker performances.<br /> <br /> Really, this is one of those concepts you can fit into basically any combination of Arcana. It just depends on what flavor you're looking for. Mind is hard to get away from if you really want the whole &quot;involuntary background singers&quot; aspect, but don't forget that ghosts and spirits also have the ability to control people, or serve as background performers in their own right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T12:56:29-07:00","id":1114248,"title":"","content":"So, is the Mage making people act as if in a musical, or is the world actually a musical?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T13:04:17-07:00","id":1114250,"title":"","content":"Bonus points: theme his fluff around music, too. His peripheral Mage Sight manifests as hearing strange melodies. His Nimbus makes him shine as if illuminated by a stage light while a catchy tune plays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T13:18:51-07:00","id":1114253,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately the intent seems the former not the later, though is a ST was able to pull that off it'd be amazingly epic. (A storyteller with wide singing and acting range, and a great troup who could sing there role? I'd pay admission to watch.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T13:51:06-07:00","id":1114261,"title":"","content":"Chronicles of Darkness: the musical. Kindred crooning out their Requiem, Uratha packs singing in chorus, Prometheans with the blues...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T14:02:43-07:00","id":1114740,"title":"","content":"Demons would sing bits of <i>Carmina Burana</i> continually. <br /> <br /> A Nimbus that literally causes people to sing was quite doable in 1e*, but in 2e, as mentioned, it can <i>also</i> help them do it <i>well</i>. <br /> (*As either Obrimos with Mind and/or Space or a Mastigos with Prime and/or Forces.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Since nobody seems to have mentioned it, yet: Familiars<br /> Shadow denizens include spirits of song and dance.<br /> Temenal beings of music and musicals would exist, too. (If nothing else, you have the muses---Terpsichore, in particular.) For that matter, some concepts of music transcend humanity, so denizens of Dreamtime could fit, too. <br /> Aether denizens may well include beings that could do this. <br /> <br /> Those with applicable Influences would love to help, since they'd feed.<br /> Adjustment in the Astral Planes could allow a person to make singing spontaneously a more normal thing in a given group, <br /> Spells that force people to sing and dance could be cast using Mind... or Fate. (They'd look a bit different.) An area effect that follows the character around and targets those minds within is a bit of a stretch for a basic mind effect. That said: An archmaster's spell or artifact could render such an effect that adapts to circumstances. <br /> The Mad could operate in a similar way, centered on their attention, for instance.<br /> An archmaster could, for some reason, simply render the entire world a musical.<br /> <br /> Man, you got choices. We talking a musical where people talk like normal for basic communication but when things get important, they burst into song? That seems like a really wacky Fate and Mind effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T09:14:40-07:00","id":1116429,"title":"","content":"Love the idea but it probably wouldn't fit to well in most chronicles. Not saying don't do it. I would love to see it happen. I think thenate's idea would be the easiest starting point. This would likely require some pretty obvious magic and a familiar could definitely help out without earning you more paradox roles then you need. Maybe play something like Mastigos with a Goetia version of andrew lloyd webber as a familiar or whatever. Then combined spells and flare your nimbus until it works for you. Make sure to set bear traps for all the Guardians of the Veil tough. If you pull this off they will likely hate your guts. Which is another kind of fun in and of itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13691-margul","name":"Margul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T11:47:56-07:00","id":1116494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Margul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1114225-silly-thought-but-i-want-to-make-a-mage-that-is-in-a-musical?p=1116429#post1116429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Love the idea but it probably wouldn't fit to well in most chronicles. Not saying don't do it. I would love to see it happen. I think thenate's idea would be the easiest starting point. This would likely require some pretty obvious magic and a familiar could definitely help out without earning you more paradox roles then you need. Maybe play something like Mastigos with a Goetia version of andrew lloyd webber as a familiar or whatever. Then combined spells and flare your nimbus until it works for you. Make sure to set bear traps for all the Guardians of the Veil tough. If you pull this off they will likely hate your guts. Which is another kind of fun in and of itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the best situation would be if you centered the whole Chronicle around it. Give the Cabal a shared identity centered around music. You could have each member represent a genre (Musical, Rock, Rap, Electronic etc.), a musician archetype (the diva, the virtuoso, the sex symbol, the busker) or my personal favorite, going whole hog on the musical theme and assigning each Cabal member a production duty - between such disparate identities as The Director, The Producer, The Composer, The Prima Donna, The Stagehand, The Usher, The Prop Master, The Stage Manager, The Sound Designer etc. etc. it's not too hard to find room for whatever archetype you might want to play.<br /> <br /> Music-themed antagonists optional but highly encouraged. Perhaps a Seer (Shadow Name: &quot;The Man&quot;) from the Ministry of Mammon constantly tempting the cabal to sell out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T12:40:21-07:00","id":1116512,"title":"","content":"For some reason, just reading the topic's name invoked my memories of that recent Supergirl/Flash crossover episode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}